exports[`git.package.patch (acceptance) given: [case1] a linked repo with is-number@7.0.0 on disk when: [t2] the crew runs \`rhx git.package.patch help\` then: the help names every subcommand, exit 0 1`] = `
"
🪨 run solid skill repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.package.patch

🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.package.patch
   ├─ subcommands
   │  ├─ begin    open an edit dir for a dependency, inside the tree
   │  ├─ commit   seal the edits into a patch + a LOCAL PATCH note
   │  └─ help     show this usage
   └─ examples
      ├─ rhx git.package.patch begin --package rhachet --mode apply
      └─ rhx git.package.patch commit --package rhachet --why 'keep the stop hook quiet on a clean tree' --upstream https://github.com/ehmpathy/rhachet/issues/580 --mode apply
"
`;

