`;

exports[`git.package.patch (acceptance) given: [case2] a linked repo with is-number@7.0.0 installed by pnpm when: [t3] a rebase drops the lockfile record, and the same commit reruns then: it names the lost record and pnpm install, never "already sealed" 1`] = `
"
🪨 run solid skill repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.package.patch

🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.package.patch commit
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: patches/is-number@7.0.0.patch and its note are present, but the lockfile record is absent, so pnpm does not apply it

🥥 did you know?
   ├─ run pnpm install, so pnpm-lock.yaml records patches/is-number@7.0.0.patch, then rerun this same commit
   └─ rhx git.package.patch commit --package is-number@7.0.0 --why 'reef fix: treat a numeric string with whitespace as not a number' --upstream https://github.com/jonschlinkert/is-number/issues/42 --mode apply
"
`;

